WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.958
SPEAKER: Google Cloud
Platform Managed Instance

00:00:01.958 --> 00:00:04.690
Groups are an easy way to set
up a group of identical servers,

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:06.520
for example web front ends.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:09.152
It can auto-scale and
auto-heal if desired.

00:00:09.152 --> 00:00:10.610
To set up a Managed
Instance Group,

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.540
start at the Compute Engine
section of the web console.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:19.851
Click Instance Groups, and
then Create Instance Group.

00:00:19.851 --> 00:00:21.850
Name your group and select
single or multi-zone.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:30.820
Now select a zone or region
and pick the instance template,

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.780
or create a new template.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.280
I want an auto-scaling group,
so I select Auto-scaling

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.736
and set the min
and max instances

00:00:38.736 --> 00:00:39.860
in the auto-scaling metric.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:48.520
If you'd like the group
to be auto-healing,

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.570
set up a health check.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:52.760
Now click Create.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:55.010
Now you have a group of
instances that will auto-scale

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:57.300
and auto-heal as needed.

